{
  "id": "oksanas-counter",
  "name": "Oksana's",
  "description": "Oksana's counter at the foot of Pylon Forty, cut into the concrete where a maintenance bay used to be, raised on a concrete step and open to the street under the Spine's deck behind a rolled-up steel shutter. Six steel stools, a zinc counter worn bright, a tall steel tea urn with a red light, a range with a big pot and a frying pan, shelves of tea glasses and jars, an old radio with an amber dial, fluorescent tubes, and a string of plain bulbs along the shutter. Beside it, a steel door under a caged lamp leads up into the pylon's hab rings. Overhead, the underside of the highway: girders, pipes and two orange sodium lamps. To the right, the street goes on under the deck past more pylons, and habs built from shipping containers hang from the girders on cables, their small windows lit, a cable stair climbing up to them. A parked three-wheeled delivery cart. Every heavy hauler overhead makes the glasses walk along the counter.",
